{"_id": "homepage", "_type": "homepage", "sections": [{"_key": "hero-1", "_type": "hero", "heading": "The Work Comes Home", "subheading": "African art prints from Kuma, produced on archival matte paper with pigment ink. Built for the diaspora, the continent, and rooms that need recognition.", "backgroundImage": {"_type": "imageWithAlt", "alt": ""}, "cta": {"label": "Enter Drop", "url": "/blog/drops/opening-drop"}}, {"_key": "featured-1", "_type": "featuredCollection", "title": "Opening Drop", "description": "The first release: 22 prints across portraiture, animal presence, abstraction, landscape, and witness.", "collectionHandle": "opening-drop", "maxProducts": 8}, {"_key": "editorial-1", "_type": "editorialBanner", "heading": "Paper, Ink, Arrival", "body": "Each launch print is produced on archival matte paper with pigment ink and shipped unframed so the collector decides how it enters the room.", "image": {"_type": "imageWithAlt", "alt": ""}, "cta": {"label": "Read Quality", "url": "/pages/print-quality"}}, {"_key": "newsletter-1", "_type": "newsletter", "heading": "Wait For The Next Arrival", "description": "Drop notes, new work, and the first signals from Tales of Kuma. No noise."}, {"_key": "grid-1", "_type": "productGrid", "title": "Start With These", "collectionHandle": "opening-drop", "maxProducts": 4}, {"_key": "text-1", "_type": "richText", "body": [{"_key": "text-1-0", "_type": "block", "style": "h2", "children": [{"_key": "text-1-0-0", "_type": "span", "text": "Built For Recognition", "marks": []}], "markDefs": []}, {"_key": "text-1-1", "_type": "block", "style": "normal", "children": [{"_key": "text-1-1-1", "_type": "span", "text": "Kumachi Prints begins in Kampala and travels outward. The work carries portraits, animals, ceremony, maps, laughter, silence, and the colors that arrive before language.", "marks": []}], "markDefs": []}, {"_key": "text-1-2", "_type": "block", "style": "normal", "children": [{"_key": "text-1-2-2", "_type": "span", "text": "Every print in the Opening Drop is produced on archival matte paper with pigment ink, then shipped after production. The launch collection is open, not falsely scarce. Buy because the image has already found you.", "marks": []}], "markDefs": []}, {"_key": "text-1-3", "_type": "block", "style": "normal", "children": [{"_key": "text-1-3-3", "_type": "span", "text": "Read the story", "marks": ["link-text-1-3-4"]}, {"_key": "text-1-3-5", "_type": "span", "text": " or ", "marks": []}, {"_key": "text-1-3-6", "_type": "span", "text": "start with the Opening Drop", "marks": ["link-text-1-3-7"]}, {"_key": "text-1-3-8", "_type": "span", "text": ".", "marks": []}], "markDefs": [{"_key": "link-text-1-3-4", "_type": "link", "url": "/pages/about"}, {"_key": "link-text-1-3-7", "_type": "link", "url": "/blog/drops/opening-drop"}]}]}], "seo": {"metaTitle": "Kumachi Prints - African Art Prints By Kuma", "metaDescription": "Shop the Opening Drop from Kumachi Prints: archival African art prints built for recognition, memory, and rooms with presence."}}
{"_id": "page-about", "_type": "page", "title": "About Kumachi Prints", "slug": {"_type": "slug", "current": "about"}, "body": [{"_key": "page-about-0", "_type": "block", "style": "h1", "children": [{"_key": "page-about-0-0", "_type": "span", "text": "About Kumachi Prints", "marks": []}], "markDefs": []}, {"_key": "page-about-1", "_type": "block", "style": "normal", "children": [{"_key": "page-about-1-1", "_type": "span", "text": "I make work for rooms that have been waiting to recognize themselves.", "marks": []}], "markDefs": []}, {"_key": "page-about-2", "_type": "block", "style": "normal", "children": [{"_key": "page-about-2-2", "_type": "span", "text": "Kumachi Prints is the place where that work can come home. The originals begin with paint, memory, pressure, and the old language carried in a name. The prints keep that first arrival intact: the face, the animal, the field of color, the quiet figure that refuses to become decoration only.", "marks": []}], "markDefs": []}, {"_key": "page-about-3", "_type": "block", "style": "normal", "children": [{"_key": "page-about-3-3", "_type": "span", "text": "I am interested in what a wall can hold.", "marks": []}], "markDefs": []}, {"_key": "page-about-4", "_type": "block", "style": "normal", "children": [{"_key": "page-about-4-4", "_type": "span", "text": "Not empty style. Not a borrowed idea of Africa. A print should bring a room into conversation with land, ancestry, humor, ceremony, governance, and the daily gestures people remember before they know why.", "marks": []}], "markDefs": []}, {"_key": "page-about-5", "_type": "block", "style": "h2", "children": [{"_key": "page-about-5-5", "_type": "span", "text": "The Work", "marks": []}], "markDefs": []}, {"_key": "page-about-6", "_type": "block", "style": "normal", "children": [{"_key": "page-about-6-6", "_type": "span", "text": "The launch collection moves through portraiture, animal presence, abstraction, landscape, and social witness. Some pieces speak plainly. Some keep their meaning behind the eyes.", "marks": []}], "markDefs": []}, {"_key": "page-about-7", "_type": "block", "style": "normal", "children": [{"_key": "page-about-7-7", "_type": "span", "text": "Each print is produced on archival matte paper with pigment ink. The launch format is unframed, so collectors can choose the frame, room, and scale that make sense for their own home.", "marks": []}], "markDefs": []}, {"_key": "page-about-8", "_type": "block", "style": "h2", "children": [{"_key": "page-about-8-8", "_type": "span", "text": "The Name", "marks": []}], "markDefs": []}, {"_key": "page-about-9", "_type": "block", "style": "normal", "children": [{"_key": "page-about-9-9", "_type": "span", "text": "Kumachi is one story told through several doors: the prints, the gallery, the studio, and the mythology still being built through Tales of Kuma.", "marks": []}], "markDefs": []}, {"_key": "page-about-10", "_type": "block", "style": "normal", "children": [{"_key": "page-about-10-10", "_type": "span", "text": "The prints are the first door. They are for people who want the work close enough to live with.", "marks": []}], "markDefs": []}, {"_key": "page-about-11", "_type": "block", "style": "h2", "children": [{"_key": "page-about-11-11", "_type": "span", "text": "For Collectors", "marks": []}], "markDefs": []}, {"_key": "page-about-12", "_type": "block", "style": "normal", "children": [{"_key": "page-about-12-12", "_type": "span", "text": "If you are buying from the diaspora, this is not a souvenir of somewhere else. It is recognition.", "marks": []}], "markDefs": []}, {"_key": "page-about-13", "_type": "block", "style": "normal", "children": [{"_key": "page-about-13-13", "_type": "span", "text": "If you are buying on the continent, this is not Western art trying to behave well on African walls. It starts from here.", "marks": []}], "markDefs": []}, {"_key": "page-about-14", "_type": "block", "style": "normal", "children": [{"_key": "page-about-14-14", "_type": "span", "text": "Choose the piece that holds your attention after the first look. That is usually the one.", "marks": []}], "markDefs": []}], "seo": {"metaTitle": "About Kumachi Prints", "metaDescription": "Meet Kumachi Prints, the print shop for Kuma: African art prints rooted in memory, mythology, and cultural confidence."}}
{"_id": "series-opening-drop", "_type": "series", "title": "Opening Drop", "slug": {"_type": "slug", "current": "opening-drop"}, "description": [{"_key": "series-opening-drop-0", "_type": "block", "style": "h1", "children": [{"_key": "series-opening-drop-0-0", "_type": "span", "text": "Opening Drop", "marks": []}], "markDefs": []}, {"_key": "series-opening-drop-1", "_type": "block", "style": "normal", "children": [{"_key": "series-opening-drop-1-1", "_type": "span", "text": "The first door opens with witnesses.", "marks": []}], "markDefs": []}, {"_key": "series-opening-drop-2", "_type": "block", "style": "normal", "children": [{"_key": "series-opening-drop-2-2", "_type": "span", "text": "This inaugural release brings together 22 prints from Kumachi Prints: lions and elephants, guarded faces, laughing boys, pot bearers, map memory, quiet spirits, and figures who hold more than they say. It is a curated open drop, not a limited edition claim. The work stays available while the launch collection remains active.", "marks": []}], "markDefs": []}, {"_key": "series-opening-drop-3", "_type": "block", "style": "normal", "children": [{"_key": "series-opening-drop-3-3", "_type": "span", "text": "The visual language moves between flat command and soft witness. A lion claims black space with electric blue, cadmium red, acid yellow, hot pink, and forest green. Three figures sit inside ritual geometry. A continent becomes a field of memory. Youth appears laughing, thinking, carrying, becoming.", "marks": []}], "markDefs": []}, {"_key": "series-opening-drop-4", "_type": "block", "style": "normal", "children": [{"_key": "series-opening-drop-4-4", "_type": "span", "text": "The pieces are produced on archival matte paper with pigment ink. They launch unframed so each collector can decide how the work should enter the room: quiet in a hallway, large above a sofa, or present in an office where every visitor has to ask about it.", "marks": []}], "markDefs": []}, {"_key": "series-opening-drop-5", "_type": "block", "style": "h2", "children": [{"_key": "series-opening-drop-5-5", "_type": "span", "text": "Shop By Subject", "marks": []}], "markDefs": []}, {"_key": "series-opening-drop-6", "_type": "block", "style": "normal", "children": [{"_key": "series-opening-drop-6-6", "_type": "span", "text": "Figurative and Portrait Art", "marks": ["link-series-opening-drop-6-7"]}], "markDefs": [{"_key": "link-series-opening-drop-6-7", "_type": "link", "url": "/collections/figurative-and-portrait-art"}], "listItem": "bullet"}, {"_key": "series-opening-drop-7", "_type": "block", "style": "normal", "children": [{"_key": "series-opening-drop-7-8", "_type": "span", "text": "Narrative and Storytelling Art", "marks": ["link-series-opening-drop-7-9"]}], "markDefs": [{"_key": "link-series-opening-drop-7-9", "_type": "link", "url": "/collections/narrative-and-storytelling-art"}], "listItem": "bullet"}, {"_key": "series-opening-drop-8", "_type": "block", "style": "normal", "children": [{"_key": "series-opening-drop-8-10", "_type": "span", "text": "Landscape and Nature", "marks": ["link-series-opening-drop-8-11"]}], "markDefs": [{"_key": "link-series-opening-drop-8-11", "_type": "link", "url": "/collections/landscape-and-nature"}], "listItem": "bullet"}, {"_key": "series-opening-drop-9", "_type": "block", "style": "normal", "children": [{"_key": "series-opening-drop-9-12", "_type": "span", "text": "Abstract Art", "marks": ["link-series-opening-drop-9-13"]}], "markDefs": [{"_key": "link-series-opening-drop-9-13", "_type": "link", "url": "/collections/abstract-art"}], "listItem": "bullet"}, {"_key": "series-opening-drop-10", "_type": "block", "style": "normal", "children": [{"_key": "series-opening-drop-10-14", "_type": "span", "text": "Contemporary African Art", "marks": ["link-series-opening-drop-10-15"]}], "markDefs": [{"_key": "link-series-opening-drop-10-15", "_type": "link", "url": "/collections/contemporary-african-art"}], "listItem": "bullet"}, {"_key": "series-opening